179→const whenToUse = `**IMPORTANT: Always check project state via memo BEFORE doing anything.**
180→
181→No matter what task you are working on - coding, debugging, refactoring, or answering questions - you MUST first use memo to understand the current project state. This ensures you have accurate, up-to-date context before making any changes or decisions.
182→
183→**When to use:**
184→- BEFORE writing any code: understand the architecture and existing patterns
185→- BEFORE debugging: check known issues and module relationships
186→- BEFORE refactoring: understand interfaces and dependencies
187→- BEFORE answering questions: get accurate project overview
